y with only one pair on a coordinated board against an opponent who showed pre-flop strength.\n\n**Option 5: Fold (-1)** - No reason to fold when checking is available.\n\n## Reason\n\nGiven that:\n1. I have a marginal one-pair hand (Jacks) on a dangerous board with overcards\n2. Opponent showed strength pre-flop but checked the turn\n3. There's one more card to come (the river)\n4. I'm not pot-committed\n5. Checking costs me nothing and lets me see the river\n\n**The optimal play is to check.** This controls the pot size with a vulnerable hand, allows me to see if the river improves my hand or completes obvious draws, and keeps me from getting raised off a hand that might be good. If opponent has a draw, I'm not giving them free odds since the pot is already substantial. If they have me beat, I minimize losses.\n\n## Answer\n0"}
