ropriate (about 60-70% of the pot of ~2,000 chips).\n\nReason: \nWith A-K on this board, I have overcards and position advantage from my pre-flop aggression. A continuation bet serves multiple purposes: it can fold out hands like low pairs, flush draws, or weaker aces, while maintaining my story of strength. If called, I still have 6 outs to top pair on the turn and river. Checking would be too passive and invite pressure from my opponent. Since I'm leading in the tournament and this is the penultimate hand, controlled aggression is optimal.\n\nAnswer: 1200"}
